Observation: {"row_count": 20, "truncated": false, "rows": [{"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "I really like their shrimp burrito and vegetarian tacos. Their 3 meat taco is pretty awesome too. Went there for lunch the other day and they were in the process of making like 80+ orders for a huge lunch, it was all hands on deck there!! And I still felt like I didn\u2019t wait longer than normal and was not treated like they were rushed. Great food, great employees."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Tacos and service were awesome. Burrito was my favorite"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "8 dollars for a killer carnitas burrito, friendly staff. I am definitely adding this to the rotation!"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Shrimp burrito, lengua taco, birria taco, el chingon, fish taco. All superb. And their rice and beans too! I'd love to try other menu items, but am having a hard time not ordering the above because they're so good!"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Run don\u2019t walk to Santos Tacos! We tried the steak, al pastor, pork carnitas, and the 3 meat fajita tacos. We also had a carne asada Mulita and the carne asada fries...and we took a burrito to go. Everything was fresh and delicious! The service was fast and friendly. We loved both the green and red salsas and we will definitely go back. The Mulita was my absolute favorite thing. Highly recommended!"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Loved it. Had the steak burrito and enjoyed the excellent service. My Mexican wife loved her pozole as well."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Customer service \u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f \u2b50\ufe0f\nFlavor \u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\nMusic \u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\nAmbiance \u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\u2b50\ufe0f\n\nI can not recommend this place enough!\nUpon arrival the owner immediately I formed us of there burrito special. Buy one burrito get the second burrito free. We ordered burritos se al pastor and pollo. Tacos de nopal and calabaza and lastly flautas.  Each plate was DELICIOUS. Each plate came with it\u2019s own Salsa. These salsa containers were very large! Had more than enough to take home. As we left the owner wished us well and a good day."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Santo Taco is by far my favorite taqueria in the valley. I had the good fortune of attending their opening and since that day, I've never had a disappointing meal there. My favorite tacos are the cabeza, al pastor, nopal and pescado. The carne asada burrito is the best in the state. Always friendly service and great food. It would be nice though if hipsters weren't always there en masse."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Simple fast food type decor with TASTY tacos. I haven't tried the burritos yet but I can't wait to go back."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "I wanted to cry when I found this place. I\u2019ve had a hard time finding good birria in SLC, let alone UT. All the food is amazing and will not disappoint, but the birria tacos are my favorite. Eat them fresh at the restaurant for maximum crispiness. I at least come here a couple times a week. I would forever die happy if you featured chilaquiles as a special one day."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Friendly people great food. Santo Taco\u2019s is my go to spot for tacos and burritos in Salt Lake."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "This place hasn\u2019t even officially opened and I\u2019m already a regular. Everything I\u2019ve tried is delicious, but the fish tacos and horchata are especially great. The veggie options are surprisingly tasty too. The atmosphere is bright and clean, and the staff are all super friendly and helpful. Come hungry and plan to come back often."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "So delicious! We got pozole on a Thursday which means all you can eat pozole but it was so much after you put the veggies on top that we could only eat one bowl! We also got the flan as a dessert and it was very creamy and delicious! I would totally recommend it! Five stars!"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "This place is hands-down the best taco place that I have found since moving to the salt lake area. There are extremely authentic and have a bunch of choices. It's two bucks for a taco, 4 bucks for a burrito, and I think four bucks for carne asada fries."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "This far, my favorite asada burrito in town."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "I live in Austin, Texas while my brother moved to Salt Lake City from San Antonio recently to pursue a great job opportunity. He swore by Santo Taco and insisted on taking my gf and I there within minutes of us leaving the airport! I never doubted that SLC is home to a great number of outstanding eateries and I\u2019m proud to report that Santo Taco contributes to this idea in Spades. I enjoyed their grilled chicken burrito and carne asada fries. If I\u2019m being honest, one of those items alone is enough to be a meal for one person or two children. My food was made to order. House made salsas, garnishes and vegetables were wonderfully fresh and the savory chicken, carne asada and salsas were a sublime compliment to the crunch of the fresh vegetables. My gf ordered the pastor taco and the asada fries and immediately went \u201cTasmanian Devil\u201d on the taco. As a testament to the portions, the asada fries went back to our hotel with us where it was later enjoyed the next day. I look forward to making it a tradition to visit Santo Taco any time I visit SLC. If you live here and haven\u2019t been, I\u2019m putting my hands on my hips and shaking my head at you. Go there already!"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Our favorite taco spot in SLC.  LOVE this fish tacos.  All the tacos are fantastic.  Burritos are huge and on point as well.  Throw in the fact the staff is incredible and this spot is a must visit.\n\nEnjoy!"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "The birria tacos are the best, I also love the pescado taco. Can't wait to go back and have more,  I want to try a birria burrito, and a el pastor taco. I will be back, oh I will be back!"}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Absolutely amazing. Quality food. The flavors are literally perfect. We ordered a burrito, mulita, birria tacos, normal tacos, a quesadilla and churros. Nothing was bad. The salsa was perfect. The meat was tender. The cheese couldn\u2019t have melted better. Churros were warm and fresh. The only negative is that it\u2019s so far from me!! \ud83d\ude29 So if they could come to southern salt lake county that would be perfect. 10/10 would recommend."}, {"name": "Santo Taco", "address": "Santo Taco, 910 900 W, Salt Lake City, UT 84116", "avg_rating": 4.6, "num_of_reviews": 758, "rating": 5.0, "text": "Great food and prices- the burritos and carne asada fries were amazing!"}]}

Action: run_sql({'query': "SELECT \n    e.name,\n    e.address,\n    e.slchd_establishment_key,\n    COUNT(i.inspection_id) as num_inspections,\n    AVG(i.inspection_score) as avg_score,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN vc.critical THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) as total_critical_violations\nFROM establishments e\nLEFT JOIN inspections i ON e.slchd_establishment_key = i.slchd_establishment_key\nLEFT JOIN violations v ON i.inspection_id = v.inspection_id\nLEFT JOIN violation_codes vc ON v.violation_code_id = vc.violation_code_id\nWHERE e.address LIKE '%84116%' OR e.name LIKE '%Santo Taco%' OR e.name LIKE '%Mestizo%' OR e.name LIKE '%Red Iguana%' OR e.name LIKE '%Chubby%' OR e.name LIKE '%Nico%' OR e.name LIKE '%Jaripeo%'\nGROUP BY e.name, e.address, e.slchd_establishment_key\nORDER BY num_inspections DESC\nLIMIT 20"})

